{
  "rationale": "The design separates sensing and motion capability in the plant, then uses deterministic specifications to enforce a conservative exploration policy. Clear conditions bias toward coverage via random_walk and short forward pulses, while any obstacle event immediately routes to dedicated turn-recovery states. Because uncontrollables are processed before controllables and motion commands are open-loop pulses, action states self-loop on non-critical path_clear and only obstacle events preempt them. Recovery returns to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed, and full_rotate is reserved only for a dedicated blocked-front escape state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model sensors and motion as separate plant automata with only the given events",
    "Use one policy automaton with small helper states: clear exploration, forward pulse, left/right/front recovery, and last-resort full scan",
    "Ensure every state is total on uncontrollable events and every non-terminal state enables exactly one controllable action",
    "Bias safe exploration toward random_walk in clear/search states and use move_forward only in a dedicated short-progress state"
  ],
